# Ship every change as a pull request

When the user asks for a change in this repo, finish by opening a pull request against `master`. That request is the authorization to commit and push the branch. They squash-merge it themselves. Do not merge, and do not wait to be asked to commit or open the PR.

Skip this for questions, reviews, explanations, and any request that does not change the repo.

## How

1. Branch from up-to-date `origin/master`. Name the branch for what the change does.
2. Make the change, including callers, tests, and fixtures it breaks.
3. Commit only the files for that change. Message style matches recent commits: one sentence about why, ending with a period.
4. Push the branch and open the PR with `gh pr create`. Base is `master`. Title is the squash commit they will land. Body is a short summary and a test-plan checklist.
5. Reply with the PR URL.

Do not push to `master`. Leave unrelated working-tree changes out of the commit. Do not commit secrets.
